# Copy this file to .env.local and fill it in. .env.local is gitignored and never committed.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# The bot does NOT need a key. Without one it answers every supported question using its keyword
# matcher — that is how the whole test suite runs, and the fallback the widget drops to any time a key
# is missing, rate-limited, or the network is down. A key only upgrades how well it understands unusual
# phrasings (and, with data-conversational, lets it phrase replies more naturally).

# OpenRouter key used for intent classification.
#
# WARNING: this is baked into dist/north-star-bot.js at build time, and anything in a browser bundle is
# public. Anyone who opens devtools can read it. Only ever put a key here that is:
#   - disposable (you will delete it when the job ends)
#   - spend-capped (set a hard monthly limit in the OpenRouter dashboard)
#   - short-expiry (set a hard expiry date)
#
# Leave it empty to build a bundle with no key in it at all.
NORTHSTAR_DEMO_KEY=
